# In S13 "the unlearned" are those still ignorant of what they are being taught.
# S17's "not the unlearned" opposes them to the clever boys of S16, so "unlearned" there means dull.
# The ignorant can learn while the dull do not, so C1 and O1 can both be true.
# "learn" may also shift, between acquiring knowledge (S5–S13) and grasping a dictation (S15–S17). It does not change the sense of any listed claim, which is why no line marks it.
